# nopekit:begin
# Written by nopekit: bytecode from importing model/, gates/ and selftest/,
# the readiness report `nopekit report --write` renders, the packages
# `nopekit export` writes, and the editor launch entry `nopekit init` writes
# with this machine's paths. Outputs, never sources.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
/REPORT.md
/out/
/.vscode/launch.json
# nopekit:end

# The page is built on demand: nopekit site init, then nopekit site build. Its text
# is tracked, and so are the baked data, the figures and the evidence copies of the
# last full round: the OpenFOAM run behind them takes about an hour, and a clone
# without OpenFOAM or ParaView shows its results from these. A clone's site build
# keeps the evidence copies it finds (it cannot copy them again: the run's own
# files are in the ignored .nopekit/out/). The page's own files, the build time and
# the live 3D file stay out.
# What slipped through (review of the first round): the evidence copies (about
# 4 MB of logs, far less in git) stayed out, so in a clone the page linked 70
# files that were not there, and its site build marked 8 numbers of the story as
# matched by nothing: they matched only the summary.json copies.
/site/*
!/site/content/
!/site/data/
/site/data/build.json
!/site/assets/
/site/assets/*
!/site/assets/figures/
!/site/assets/evidence/
